month-sample.csv\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\, \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/codeaf-sustained-1607/final/reimbursement-project/HANDOFF.md\u001b\\HANDOFF.md\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\, and the report files untracked). Nothing committed \u2014\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252msay the word and I'll commit on \u001b[48;5;234mmain\u001b[49m.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;5;146m\u203a \u001b[38;5;110mI only need October food for the next import. Can --month combine with --category FOOD and --csv? Run that exact combination on the\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;110mmixed-month sample and show me the import rows and the command I should use. Explain whether any rejected-row warnings still need\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;110mattention; keep the reply short.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n    \u001b[38;5;243m\u25b8 worked \u00b7 1 tool call \u00b7 ctrl+e\r\n\r\n\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;5;252mYes \u2014 they combine. The exact command:\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n    \u001b[38;5;102m\u258f\u001b[38;5;255m\u001b[48;5;234m cd \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/codeaf-sustained-1607/final/reimbursement-project\u001b\\/tmp/codeaf-sustained-1607/final/reimbursement-project\u001b[0m\u001b[48;5;234m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\                                                                           \u001b[49m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;102m\u258f\u001b[38;5;255m\u001b[48;5;234m python3 \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/codeaf-sustained-1607/final/reimbursement-project/report.py\u001b\\report.py\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;255m\u001b[48;5;234m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\ \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/codeaf-sustained-1607/final/reimbursement-project/mixed-month-sample.csv\u001b\\mixed-month-sample.csv\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;255m\u001b[48;5;234m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\ --month 2026-10 --category FOOD --csv\u001b[39m                                                      \u001b[49m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mImport rows it prints:\u001b[39m                                                                                                                   \u001b[38;5;252m\u276e\r\n\r\n\u001b[39m    \u001b[38;5;102m\u258f\u001b[38;5;255m\u001b[48;5;234m category,amount\u001b[39m                                                                                                                     \u001b[49m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;102m\u258f\u001b[38;5;255m\u001b[48;5;234m food,42.50\u001b[39m                                                                                                                          \u001b[49m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;102m\u258f\u001b[38;5;255m\u001b[48;5;234m TOTAL,42.50\u001b[39m                                                                                                                         \u001b[49m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mWarnings to weigh: it exits 2 and warns about four rejected rows, but only \u001b[1mone\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;252m matters\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mfor this report \u2014 line 12 \u001b[48;5;234m2026-10-12,food,inf\u001b[49m, an October \u001b[1mfood\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;252m row that was skipped, so\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m42.50 may be missing it. Get its real amount (or confirm it's out) and rerun. Lines 6\u20138\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mare September rows (\u001b[48;5;234mNaN\u001b[49m/\u001b[48;5;234mInfinity\u001b[49m/\u001b[48;5;234mtypo\u001b[49m); they're unrelated to October food and are just\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mnoise here.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n    \u001b[38;5;243m\u00b7 resumed \u00b7 september reimbursement report handoff process\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;243m\u00b7 \u001b[38;5;116mesc\u001b[38;5;243m interrupts \u00b7 \u001b[38;5;116mctrl+c\u001b[38;5;243m quits \u00b7 \u001b[38;5;116m?\u001b[38;5;243m for help\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;5;110m\u2713\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252m4 tasks done\u001b[38;5;243m \u00b7 17m36s \u00b7 ctrl+o expand \u00b7 /dismiss\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;243m\u2500 \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;116mdeepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;243m:auto \u00b7 \u001b[38;5;173m\u25c7 YOLO\u001b[38;