b[38;5;243m quits \u00b7 \u001b[38;5;116m?\u001b[38;5;243m for help\u001b[39m                                                                                           \u001b[38;5;252m\u276e\r\n\r\n\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;5;110m\u2713\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252m4 tasks done\u001b[38;5;243m \u00b7 17m36s \u00b7 ctrl+o expand \u00b7 /dismiss\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;5;146m\u203a \u001b[38;5;110mThe October food result was provisional because a row was rejected. I want to automate finance imports and cannot let a partial\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;110mreport look complete. Add an opt-in --strict mode: if any row would be skipped, emit the warnings but no report on stdout and exit 2.\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;110mGood data should still produce the report. First give me a short human-facing progress update after inspecting the current behavior,\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;110mthen continue implementing and testing this. Update the handoff with the safe import command.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252madding --strict tests\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mdocumenting the safe import command in the handoff\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mfinal verification and cleanup\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;238m\u25aa verifying final state in reimbursement-project directory\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;103m\u25aa --strict is in, tested, and documented\u001b[39m                                                                            \u001b[38;5;238m\u2191\u001b[38;5;252m 54.7k\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;5;238m\u2193\u001b[38;5;252m 9,060\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;243m\u2500 \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;116mdeepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;243m (together):auto \u00b7 \u001b[38;5;173m\u25c7 YOLO\u001b[38;5;243m \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 \u001b[39m   \u001b[38;5;252m$0.34\u001b[38;5;243m \u00b7 \u001b[38;5;252m\u27f2 saved $0.1138 \u00b7 86% cached\u001b[38;5;243m   \u001b[38;5;252m54.7k/1M \u00b7 5%\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;5;146m\u2834\u001b[39